      "message": "When using the response struct it will be more like\n\n       /* Wait for response from Cr50 */\n\tfor (i \u003d 0; i \u003c sizeof(res); i++) {\n                uint8_t *buffer \u003d (uint8_t*)\u0026res;\n\t\twhile (!timeout) {\n\t\t\tint c \u003d uart_getc();\n\t\t\t// If nothing is ready (-1), try polling again in 1ms\n\t\t\tif (c !\u003d -1) {\n\t\t\t\tbuffer[i] \u003d c;\n\t\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tmsleep(1);\n\t\t\ttimeout \u003d timestamp_expired(until, NULL);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\n\nThen we can access return code with\n\nres.return_code;",
